{"name":"Bandana","hex":"#01578f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bandana","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large kerchief, usually colourful and used either as headgear or as a handkerchief, neckerchief, bikini, or sweatband.","A style of calico printing, in which white or bright spots are produced upon cloth previously dyed a uniform red or dark colour, by discharging portions of the color by chemical means, while the rest of the cloth is under pressure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bandana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bandana (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Bandana is the second collaborative studio album by American rapper Freddie Gibbs and record producer Madlib. It was released on June 28, 2019, by ESGN, Keep Cool Records, Madlib Invazion, and RCA Records. Entirely produced by Madlib, it is the follow-up to their critically acclaimed 2014 album Piñata, and their sixth overall project as a duo. The album features guest appearances from Pusha T, Killer Mike, Anderson .Paak, Yasiin Bey, and Black Thought."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b5/Bandana_freddie_gibbs.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bandana_(album)"},{"title":"Bandana (pop band)","blocks":[{"text":"Bandana is an Argentine pop girl group formed in 2001. Following the international trend of teen pop girl groups established by the Spice Girls, the five members of Bandana — Ivonne Guzmán, Lourdes Cecilia Fernández, Valeria Gastaldi, Virginia Da Cunha and María Elizabeth Vera — were selected on the TV show Popstars and were a carefully marketed product that became a phenomenon in the country, particularly among young girls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Recital.jpg/330px-Recital.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bandana_(pop_band)"},{"title":"Kerchief","blocks":[{"text":"A kerchief, also known as a bandana or bandanna, is a triangular or square piece of cloth tied around the head, face, or neck for protective or decorative purposes. The popularity of head kerchiefs may vary by culture or religion, often being used as a Christian headcovering by men and women of the Anabaptist, Eastern Orthodox, and Plymouth Brethren denominations, as well as by some Orthodox Jewish and Muslim men and women and is also considered a hat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Ari%27s_back.jpg/330px-Ari%27s_back.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kerchief"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Red_and_blue_bandannas.jpg/250px-Red_and_blue_bandannas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Red_and_blue_bandannas.jpg/500px-Red_and_blue_bandannas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Red_and_blue_bandannas.jpg/250px-Red_and_blue_bandannas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_and_blue_bandannas.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Bandanas.jpg/250px-Bandanas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Bandanas.jpg/500px-Bandanas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Bandanas.jpg/250px-Bandanas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABandanas.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb